y would look like  is i want to take this picture and i  want to convert that into this  i have my business logic now abstracted  away from all of my network functions my  identity my observability my policies my  authentication and authorization  since we live in the world of containers  we can toss both of those things in the  container  and in kubernetes we can put multiple  containers inside of a pod  now this is called a sidecar pattern  where you have kind of your primary  container that's your application  container that's running up  and then you have kind of a sidecar  container that's providing additional  functionality to that primary container  and that sidecar container suspiciously  looks like a network proxy because it's  providing a lot of network functions  envoy is a very popular proxy that's  used in distributed system that's used  for client-side load balancing because  now i'm going to slap this envoy proxy  to every single container there are a  lot of operational benefits to this too  i have a very clear kind of lines of  delineation between roles and  responsibility on who's doing what  above this blue line is my business  logic are my application developers  they can just now focus on developing  the application below this line are my  operators  they can focus on building the platform  putting policies on the platform and  forcing those policies  this is to me the kind of the true  definition of portability this container  now can run anywhere  as long as those functions is provided  by the platform and now i've relegated  these additional network functions onto  the platform layer  that are managed by experts that know  how to manage networks how to manage  security how to manage observability  so let's look at an implementation of  this how do we implement this thing  istio and anto service mesh are just two  of the implementation  istio is an open source implementation  of a office service mesh  anthos is a google managed service mesh  t